Final Remarks

This exploratory data analysis project investigated pricing patterns, market composition, and listing characteristics across Airbnb properties. 
By combining data cleaning pipelines with descriptive statistics, the key findings are:

1. Market Concentration & Geographic Price Disparity
Listing Distribution: India (2,779), Italy (1,187), and Greece (889) represent the highest listing volumes on the platform.
Pricing Divergence: European markets (Italy at 31,636 and Greece at 31,432 avg price) command more than 4x the daily rates seen in Asian markets like 
India (7,537 avg price).

2. Amenities (Pool & Pet-Friendly Policies)
Properties offering amenities like swimming pools or pet-friendly accommodations average 21,110 per night, compared to 13,608 for standard listings.
This represents a +55.1% price (+7,502 in absolute), indicating willingness to pay for flexibility features.

3. Review Ratings Do Not Drive Daily Rates
The correlation between numerical review scores and listing price is virtually nonexistent (r = 0.079).
While listings with lower ratings (< 4.0) initially appear to have higher average prices (25,026), median price comparisons (9,000–9,700) prove this is 
heavily distorted by extreme luxury outliers in a small sample. Daily pricing is fundamentally set by location and listing capacity, not user review scores.

4. Host Concentration & Competitive Volume Strategy
Single-property hosts dominate the platform supply (69.7% share vs. 30.3% for multi-property hosts).
Despite multi-hosts owning premium portfolio assets that push up their average prices (18,931 vs. 17,161), their median prices are slightly lower 
(7,942 vs. 8,211), suggesting a competitive pricing strategy.

5. Group Economies of Scale vs. Large Estate Premiums
Economies of Scale: Booking listings for 3–6 guests delivers maximum per-person efficiency, reducing the median cost per guest by 30% to 40% compared to couples.
Luxury Inflection Point: Once listings exceed 4 bedrooms, the cost-per-guest trend reverses, climbing above 2,500–3,100 as listings shift from residential spaces
into premium villas and estates.

Technical Implementation Highlights
 - Data Cleaning: Whitespace stripping on categorical text columns, converted mixed-type ratings (`'New'` string to `NaN`), and imputed missing values in check-out
schedules.
- Extracted boolean tags from string-formatted amenities, segmented hosts via frequency mapping, created binned rating tiers, and generated per-guest cost 
efficiency metrics.
- Aggregation: Utilized both mean and median metrics to ensure distributions and outlier listings did not compromise business conclusions.
